    {
      "kind": "source",
      "text": "The paper frames the issue with a simple grid of variable-use rules. A bound variable is an occurrence owned by a surrounding λ—the x in λx.x, for example. Start from the linear calculus, where every bound variable appears exactly once. Then allow omission, repetition, or both.",
